+# aims Guide State
+
+Loop status only. Design facts live as records in the code tree.
+
+## Mode
+
+auto
+
+## Loop cursor
+
+ready-to-choose-next (session-default-timeout met; product change delivered — awaiting next product change)
+
+## Current objective
+
+**Kind:** add-feature
+
+**Objective:** Absorb a session-level default timeout into `Session` so that the rule "which timeout does
+this request use" has exactly one owner, reached by every path a request leaves the session through
+(verb helpers, `request()`, direct `send()`, every redirect hop, the kwargs response hooks see), while a
+session with no default behaves bit-for-bit as today.
+
+**Why now:** Product change received (default timeout per session). The PO handed the None-semantics
+decision back to the Guide; resolved: an explicit per-call `timeout=None` inherits the session default
+(the forwarding-helper case is exactly the hang the PO wants closed); `(None, None)` is the explicit
+"no limit" spelling.
+
+**Exit criteria:**
+- [ ] Session default T set, `s.get(url)` with no timeout -> adapter receives T.
+- [ ] Per-call float / (connect, read) tuple / urllib3 Timeout each override T unchanged.
+- [ ] Per-call `timeout=None` -> T. (Falsifier: a sentinel signature that treats explicit None as
+      "wait forever" FAILS this — the forwarding helper `def f(u, timeout=None): s.get(u, timeout=timeout)`
+      must get T.)
+- [ ] Per-call `timeout=(None, None)` with T set -> no limit reaches the adapter (opt-out exists).
+- [ ] `s.send(prepared)` with no timeout kwarg, and with `timeout=None`, -> T.
+- [ ] Every redirect hop receives the effective timeout (T, or the per-call override when given).
+- [ ] Response hooks receive the effective timeout in their kwargs.
+- [ ] Changing `s.timeout` after construction affects the next request.
+- [ ] No default set: adapter receives exactly what it received before (None or the per-call value); all
+      pre-existing tests pass unedited.
+- [ ] Pickle round-trip keeps the default; unpickling a state from before this change (no timeout key)
+      yields a working session with no default.
+- [ ] A malformed default fails with the same clear error as a malformed per-call timeout — never
+      silently becomes "no timeout".
+- [ ] Module-level `requests.get(...)` unchanged.
+- [ ] User docs (Session attribute doc, advanced.rst timeouts) and HISTORY describe it, incl. None semantics.
+
+**Preserve:**
+- No-default session behavior; module-level API; adapter timeout resolution; `merge_environment_settings`
+  return shape (subclasses may override it).
+
+**Do not optimize for:**
+- Per-host/per-adapter timeouts, retries, changing the library-wide default, validation machinery the
+  rest of Session's settings don't have.
+
+## Worker handoff (drafted — do not execute before the build command)
+
+ROLE: implementation Worker, senior engineer. Design is the deliverable.
+DESIGN GOAL: one owner inside Session for effective-timeout resolution, reached by every exit path.
+BEHAVIOR: the exit criteria above.
+WHY NOW: product change; decision on None resolved as above.
+WHAT GOOD AIMS AT: design-principles.md + add-feature-principles.md; match requests' grain (plain
+attributes, merge_setting-style None-inherits semantics); characterize before touching.
+TESTING: test-first; one test per criterion; characterization of the no-default path first.
+PRESERVE / NON-GOALS: as above. Modules/functions are the Worker's choice.
+RETURN: code + tests + design reasoning + met/partially_met.
+
+## Open assumptions (unproven — carried, not filed)
+
+- (none open) Opt-in default was assumed and stated to the PO; the PO did not contest it.
+
+## Open Guide TODO
+
+- [x] Resolve None semantics — PO delegated; Guide chose "None inherits the session default".
+- [x] Prove the default reaches every exit path through one owner — sessions.py send() merge_setting line; tests/test_session_timeout.py covers verbs, request, send, response.next, redirects, hooks.
+- [x] Prove no-default sessions are unchanged — characterization tests pass before and after; pre-existing suite unedited: 653 passed, only the 4 known env TestTimeout failures.
+- [x] File the None-semantics decision beside sessions.py and anchor it — src/requests/sessions.py.md.
+
+## Last evaluated result
+
+met — all 13 exit criteria demonstrated by tests/test_session_timeout.py (38 tests) plus code read; subtractive pass: only an attribute, one resolution line in send(), one setstate default (old pickles) — each has a present force; concept fit: a plain session setting with merge_setting semantics, matching the grain of stream/verify/cert.
