@@ -1120,6 +1120,26 @@ coffee.
 
     r = requests.get('https://github.com', timeout=None)
 
+Session default timeout
+^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
+
+Rather than repeating ``timeout=`` on every call, you can set a default once on
+a :class:`~requests.Session`. Every request sent through that session uses it,
+including each redirect it follows, unless the request passes its own
+``timeout``::
+
+    s = requests.Session()
+    s.timeout = (3.05, 27)
+
+    s.get('https://github.com')              # uses (3.05, 27)
+    s.get('https://github.com', timeout=5)   # uses 5
+
+On a session with a default, ``timeout=None`` also means "use the session
+default", so a helper that forwards an unset timeout cannot hang. To make one
+request wait forever on such a session, pass ``(None, None)``::
+
+    s.get('https://github.com', timeout=(None, None))
+
 .. note:: The connect timeout applies to each connection attempt to an IP address.
           If multiple addresses exist for a domain name, the underlying ``urllib3`` will
           try each address sequentially until one successfully connects.
